{"interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory","stdout":"════ master_dependencies abstract ════\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis is the single source of truth for the logical status of the Collatz program across its three\nmanuscripts.  Its purpose is to prevent overclaiming: it states exactly what is proved, what is a\nproof sketch, what is numerical evidence, what is imported, and what is open.  \\textbf{The headline\ncorrection:} the program has \\emph{not} reduced Collatz to a single problem.  Collatz is currently\n\\emph{not} known to be equivalent to SRCE.  The honest statement is the one-directional conditional\nreduction\n\\[\n  \\mathrm{SRCE}\\ +\\ \\text{Exit Inequality}\\ +\\ \\text{cycle elimination}\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\text{Collatz},\n\\]\nwhich decomposes into the four open inputs catalogued below.  After two of those inputs were\ndischarged to finite, checkable form (H2 became a finite admissible-block verification; the depth\nscale R3 was settled at the diffusive $O((\\log P)^2)$, i.e.\\ finite), the remaining \\emph{analytic}\ncontent collapses to a single statement---the \\textbf{Unified Sparse-Target Equidistribution\nConjecture} (\\S\\ref{sec:unified})---which is this program's true endpoint and a candidate piece of\nnew mathematics.  No claim of a proof of the Collatz conjecture is made anywhere in this program;\nthe contribution is to have located, sharply stated, and reduced Collatz to that conjecture modulo\nthe catalogued proved/numerical/imported inputs.\n\\end{abstract}\n════ pointwise_valuation abstract ════\n\\begin{abstract}\nThe accelerated (Syracuse) Collatz map on odd integers is\n$S(x) = (3x+1)/2^{\\vv(3x+1)}$, with accelerated valuation $b(x) = \\vv(3x+1)$.  Under\nthe natural Haar law on the $2$-adic integers the valuations are independent,\nidentically distributed (i.i.d.)\\ geometric with mean $\\E[b] = 2 > \\log_2 3$, so a\ntypical orbit descends; the Collatz difficulty is the upgrade of this\nmeasure-theoretic statement to a single deterministic orbit.  We isolate that upgrade\nas a standalone dynamical statement---the weak \\emph{Pointwise Valuation Theorem}\n(PVT), the sole pointwise input to a bounded-deficit reduction of the Collatz\nconjecture modulo cycle elimination---and prove its \\emph{annealed} version with an\nexplicit, machine-checked Lyapunov function (a correction-weighted, floor-killed\ntransfer operator of spectral radius $\\le \\sqrt3/(2\\sqrt2-1) < 1$).  Our main\ncontribution is a reduction and localization: using an explicit canonical-residue\nformula $r_m \\equiv 3^{-m}(2^{D_m}-A_m)\\pmod{2^{D_m+1}}$ we show the weak PVT is\n\\emph{equivalent} to a deterministic shrinking-target statement, which we isolate as\nthe \\emph{Stabilized Residue Cluster Extinction Problem}: no fixed odd $x_0$ admits an\ninfinite valuation word whose canonical residues stabilize to $x_0$ while the\ndeficit stays confined, $D_m - m\\log_2 3 \\le C$.  We then eliminate, by proof or by\ncomputation, every natural mechanism that might force this---finite-state and block\nLyapunov functions, Baker/convergent near-cycle control, word-level entropy and\ncomplexity, $\\times2,\\times3$ entropy rigidity and reblocking, $p$-adic scenery\noverlap, and mod-$4$/restart-density arguments---and explain precisely why the\nprobabilistic heuristic is not a proof: the confined counterexample word is\nsymbolically generic (indistinguishable from a confined renewal word in all word\nstatistics), the residue map is per-scale uniform with summable targets $\\asymp\n3^{-m}$, but the deterministic target hits are maximally clustered, because the lift\ndigits are nonnegative and the residue is monotone.  The confined-run length has a\ngeometric survival law ($\\rho \\approx 0.93$) and a bounded extreme-value record ratio,\n════ sparse_target_inverse_theorem abstract ════\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis note records the corrected pivot suggested by the current state of the SRCE/PVT/Exit program.  The remaining obstruction is not finite-state dynamics, local valuation algebra, transfer-graph rank, bounded symbolic grammar, or an annealed Borel--Cantelli estimate.  It is a deterministic sparse-target avoidance problem for a non-invertible affine cocycle.  The purpose of this note is to formulate a concrete inverse-theorem framework: persistent over-hitting of sparse targets should force a finite-character/coboundary or affine residue obstruction; the H23a/Wielandt certificate machinery is then designed to exclude precisely such obstructions.\n\nThe note deliberately avoids overclaiming.  The proposed theorem is not presently a theorem from Green--Tao nilsequence theory, Schmidt games, or homogeneous nondivergence.  Those theories are useful analogies, but the immediate Collatz-specific path is lower-level: finite Fourier analysis on \\(\\mathbb Z/2^N\\mathbb Z\\), an affine-cocycle inverse statement, and a coboundary exclusion certificate.\n\\end{abstract}\n════ stabilized_residue_extinction abstract ════\n\\begin{abstract}\nThe accelerated (Syracuse) Collatz map $S(x) = (3x+1)/2^{\\vv(3x+1)}$ on odd integers reduces---%\nconditionally on cycle elimination and an Exit Inequality, both carried by companion\npapers~\\cite{JanikPVT,Janik2026reduction}---to a single pointwise statement, equivalent to a\ndeterministic shrinking-target problem about the canonical residues\n$r_m \\equiv 3^{-m}(2^{D_m}-A_m) \\pmod{2^{D_m+1}}$ of the orbit, which we isolate as the\n\\emph{Stabilized Residue Cluster Extinction Problem} (SRCE).  Because the lift digits are\nnonnegative, $r_m$ is monotone and the hits to a fixed target are maximally clustered, so\nordinary Borel--Cantelli does not apply.  This paper is a \\emph{conditional reduction and\nlocalization}.  We represent the extremal set as a peak-rooted inverse-Syracuse tree, model it\nas a killed critical branching random walk in a strip, and reduce SRCE to a\n\\emph{fixed-modulus spectral gap} for the inverse-Syracuse congruence operator.  For the\n\\emph{annealed} operator that gap is a theorem; the arithmetic character-killing mechanism is\nidentified, verified computationally and, for the local congruence mechanisms, partially\nmachine-checked in Lean ($2$-adic characters by a block collision generating the odd-residue\ntorsor, $3$-adic by the offspring $b$-sum through the primitivity of $2$).  The remaining\nmathematical content is the \\emph{exact} residue-mode contraction (H23a): a Perron--Frobenius\nspectral gap for the exact deterministic operator with constants uniform in the strip width,\nfrom which bulk fiber equidistribution follows---together with the separate problem of cycle\nelimination.  The contribution is to\nlocalize the Collatz pointwise obstruction to this finite operator comparison; it is a\nconditional reduction, not a proof of the Collatz conjecture.  All quantitative claims are\ncomputational and labelled as such.\n\\end{abstract}"}